C++ TEMPLATES (C++11/14/17)
Interview Notes
=========================================================

1. INTRODUCTION TO TEMPLATES
============================

What are Templates?
-------------------
Templates are a compile-time feature that allows writing generic code that
works with different data types without duplicating code.

Instead of writing separate functions/classes for int, double, string, etc.,
write a single generic implementation.

Templates provide:
• Code reusability
• Type safety
• Compile-time polymorphism
• Better maintainability

---------------------------------------------------------

Without Templates

int max(int a, int b)
{
    return (a > b) ? a : b;
}

double max(double a, double b)
{
    return (a > b) ? a : b;
}

string max(string a, string b)
{
    return (a > b) ? a : b;
}

Same logic repeated multiple times.

---------------------------------------------------------

With Templates

template<typename T>
T max(T a, T b)
{
    return (a > b) ? a : b;
}

Works for:

max(10,20);
max(5.5,3.2);
max(string("ABC"), string("XYZ"));

---------------------------------------------------------

How Templates Work?

Templates are NOT actual functions/classes.

They are blueprints.

When a template is used, the compiler generates the required function/class
for that specific type. This process is called:

Template Instantiation

Example

template<typename T>
T square(T x)
{
    return x * x;
}

Calls

square(5);      // T = int
square(2.5);    // T = double

Compiler generates:

int square(int);

double square(double);

---------------------------------------------------------

Advantages

✓ Eliminates duplicate code
✓ Compile-time type checking
✓ Better performance (resolved at compile time)
✓ Easier maintenance
✓ Works with user-defined classes
✓ Foundation of STL (vector, map, list, etc.)

---------------------------------------------------------

Disadvantages

• Longer compilation time
• Larger executable (code bloat)
• Complex compiler error messages
• Implementation usually kept in header files

---------------------------------------------------------

Types of Templates

